# Gate step 1249-xngp — dev-inference-ensure.sh names the lane that SERVED
# (bare-metal or container) on every lane, with stub curl/podman: a host-native
# engine on the port is not taken for the container; with no engine at all the
# container fallback starts and says so (the negative control); macOS with no
# engine is refused with its remedy; --probe-fallback checks the container on
# the next port without touching the serving endpoint.
#
# STEP_LUA is a LITERAL path on purpose (1063-nraf).
STEP_DESC="Checking the inference readiness verdict names its serving lane (1249-xngp)"
STEP_LUA="scripts/lua/test-dev-inference-lane.lua"
STEP_ERROR="dev-inference-ensure.sh no longer names the lane that served, or its fallback probe touched the serving engine (1249-xngp) — see the FAIL lines above"
STEP_OK="Inference readiness names its serving lane"
